  "doc": "The inventory: the things a hand can hold and place, read by the VR bracelet's PLACE mode (commons/player/inventory_hand.gd) and by the encyclopedia's /catalyst-inventory prism. One item = one registry token, how it mounts (wall, floor, hand, any - or worn: a bangle on the bracelet's hand, used without holding it, as the tape is), its own defaults (the artifact's defaults stay as they are), and its knobs: each knob names an @export of the token's script (tools/inventory_check.py refuses a knob the code does not have). unlock: '' = always; a sequence id = after that sequence. scale (optional) shrinks the artifact as a whole, so a wall console becomes a hand-sized one without touching the artifact's own size. An item with 'coming' has no scene yet and shows greyed. The ball is the point and the rod the line; a rod let go near a ball's socket snaps in (playground_kit).",
